  "contract": [
    "Null config, size other than36 or interface string other than pv_v1.1.0 returns1 without altering owners. Valid calls allocate336 bytes without clearing it or checking allocation, then set native fields. Unknown modes preserve the prior allocated window word unless explicitly overridden.",
    "Rate defaults to25 then truncates16 bits before division by25. Minimum batch uses signed-positive clamp then byte truncation. Stride/terminal defaults1/202; candidate limit uses unsigned cap20. Full override words, low window byte and untouched padding preserved.",
    "All four workspace-owner words at200377a4 are cleared before allocating344 bytes into the first cell. Canonical owner storage grows from4 to16 bytes; destructor uses cell0 and retains native post-free dangling-owner behavior. No shadow owner.",
    "Context owner is reloaded after external calls. Parameter records use selectors0/1/6 and native table/code fields; callback mutation of later records and null graph returns are preserved. No guessed failure cleanup.",
    "Two byte queues allocate exactly3 bytes each, not three16-bit elements. Existing C float records allocate12 each. Four final float defaults use representation48800000; four double fields are raw zero words.",
    "830 paired cases include independent primary-field, byte-queue and call-order oracles; every440 native instruction bytes executes.128 actual C allocator/complete teardown lifecycles free primary/workspace/graph records/queues back to prior heap top."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Workspace initializer72c48, graph constructor dispatcher3ddf4 and four table getters remain unresolved. Direct tests model these and malloc; existing C float-record initializer and memory/string primitives execute.",
    "Heap lifecycles execute the actual C allocator and entire destructor chain. Three provider-owned graph records are preallocated with each real allocator and transferred through modeled graph returns; their internal construction/allocation timing and workspace internal allocations remain unproven.",
    "No allocation failure guards were invented. First allocation failure compares a logical unmapped-write fault. A null workspace allocation is only covered through the modeled workspace provider; real downstream fault behavior is not established.",
    "Saved registers/SP/masks/active FPSCR, all modeled provider snapshots, full arena contents, four-word workspace owner and guard are compared. Invalid pointers, reentrant/concurrent code, cold FP activation, private stack frames, caller scratch and physical fault widths remain outside proof.",
    "The886-unit ld-r composition has no failures or duplicate strong symbols.874 prior nongenerated source/object pairs unchanged; canonical processing teardown source/header changed only for the owner extent and cell0 access. Constructor has no new writable state; owner expansion adds12 bytes. Tested constructor and processing objects match normal build.",
    "Application imports73 to78: one high-level constructor import replaced by six lower-level dependencies. Boot remains22. Source-plan/cache layout unchanged. Final executable linking/startup, hardware delivery and boot remain open."
  ],
